{"content":[{"c":["VIRGIN"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Word used only of women and (metaphorically) of places, nations, and the church. Literally, it describes a woman who has reached physical maturity but has not experienced sexual intercourse. Mary, mother of Jesus, is an obvious example (",{"href":"?bref=Matt.1.18-25","r":"Matt.1.18-25","rawR":"Matt.1.18-25","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Matt.1.18-25","value":"Matt.1.18-25"}],"t":"ref","v":"Mt 1:18-25"},")."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"},{"c":["The OT puts a high value on premarital virginity. One of Rebekah’s qualities that made her a suitable bride for Isaac was her virginity (",{"href":"?bref=Gen.24.16","r":"Gen.24.16","rawR":"Gen.24.16","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.24.16","value":"Gen.24.16"}],"t":"ref","v":"Gn 24:16"},"). The law prescribed that priests, as men whose lives should conform most closely to God’s standards, must marry only virgins (",{"href":"?bref=Lev.21.7,13-14","r":"Lev.21.7,13-14","rawR":"Lev.21.7,13-14","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Lev.21.7,13-14","value":"Lev.21.7,13-14"}],"t":"ref","v":"Lv 21:7, 13-14"},")."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"},{"c":["Undoubtedly this reflects the whole Bible’s teaching on marriage, with its ideal of exclusive faithfulness. The NT expresses that ideal by its ban on premarital intercourse (",{"href":"?bref=1Cor.6.13,18","r":"1Cor.6.13,18","rawR":"1Cor.6.13,18","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Cor.6.13,18","value":"1Cor.6.13,18"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Cor 6:13, 18"},"), and by its use of “virgin” language to describe Christians who remain faithful to their Lord (",{"href":"?bref=Rev.14.4","r":"Rev.14.4","rawR":"Rev.14.4","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Rev.14.4","value":"Rev.14.4"}],"t":"ref","v":"Rv 14:4"},"; cf. ",{"href":"?bref=2Cor.11.2","r":"2Cor.11.2","rawR":"2Cor.11.2","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Cor.11.2","value":"2Cor.11.2"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Cor 11:2"},")."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"},{"c":["Negatively, the OT highlights the same principle in the penalties it lays down for the loss of a woman’s virginity. If the man is morally responsible, he must either marry her or compensate her father (",{"href":"?bref=Exod.22.16-17","r":"Exod.22.16-17","rawR":"Exod.22.16-17","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Exod.22.16-17","value":"Exod.22.16-17"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ex 22:16-17"},"). If the woman herself is to blame, the punishment is death (",{"href":"?bref=Deut.22.20-21","r":"Deut.22.20-21","rawR":"Deut.22.20-21","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Deut.22.20-21","value":"Deut.22.20-21"}],"t":"ref","v":"Dt 22:20-21"},"). The OT says little, however, to commend lifelong virginity. Jeremiah was told not to marry, only to reinforce God’s warning of coming judgment (",{"href":"?bref=Jer.16.2","r":"Jer.16.2","rawR":"Jer.16.2","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Jer.16.2","value":"Jer.16.2"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jer 16:2"},"). From the woman’s point of view, it was a tragedy to remain an unmarried virgin and therefore childless for life (cf. ",{"href":"?bref=Judg.11.37","r":"Judg.11.37","rawR":"Judg.11.37","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Judg.11.37","value":"Judg.11.37"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jgs 11:37"},")."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"},{"c":["The NT echoes the value of marriage but brings out more clearly the advantages of a commitment to virginity for Christian men as well as women. Celibacy for some is God’s gift, declared Paul, because it has positive gains for Christian service (",{"href":"?bref=1Cor.7.7,25-38","r":"1Cor.7.7,25-38","rawR":"1Cor.7.7,25-38","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Cor.7.7,25-38","value":"1Cor.7.7,25-38"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Cor 7:7, 25-38"},"). Jesus commended those who “make themselves eunuchs” for the kingdom of heaven’s sake (",{"href":"?bref=Matt.19.12","r":"Matt.19.12","rawR":"Matt.19.12","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Matt.19.12","value":"Matt.19.12"}],"t":"ref","v":"Mt 19:12"},")."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"},{"c":[{"c":["See also"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=FamilyLifeandRelations_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"FamilyLifeandRelations_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"FamilyLifeandRelations_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Family Life and Relations"},"; ",{"href":"?item=MarriageMarriageCustoms_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"MarriageMarriageCustoms_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"MarriageMarriageCustoms_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Marriage, Marriage Customs"},"; ",{"href":"?item=SexSexuality_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"SexSexuality_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"SexSexuality_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Sex, Sexuality"},"; ",{"href":"?item=VirginBirthofJesus_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"VirginBirthofJesus_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"VirginBirthofJesus_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Virgin Birth of Jesus"},"; ",{"href":"?item=Woman_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"Woman_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"Woman_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Woman"},"."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Virgin","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Mt 1:18-25","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Matt.1.18-25","rawQueryValue":"Matt.1.18-25","sourceRefExact":"Matt.1.18-25"},{"anchorText":"Gn 24:16","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gen.24.16","rawQueryValue":"Gen.24.16","sourceRefExact":"Gen.24.16"},{"anchorText":"Lv 21:7, 13-14","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Lev.21.7,13-14","rawQueryValue":"Lev.21.7,13-14","sourceRefExact":"Lev.21.7,13-14"},{"anchorText":"1 Cor 6:13, 18","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Cor.6.13,18","rawQueryValue":"1Cor.6.13,18","sourceRefExact":"1Cor.6.13,18"},{"anchorText":"Rv 14:4","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Rev.14.4","rawQueryValue":"Rev.14.4","sourceRefExact":"Rev.14.4"},{"anchorText":"2 Cor 11:2","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Cor.11.2","rawQueryValue":"2Cor.11.2","sourceRefExact":"2Cor.11.2"},{"anchorText":"Ex 22:16-17","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Exod.22.16-17","rawQueryValue":"Exod.22.16-17","sourceRefExact":"Exod.22.16-17"},{"anchorText":"Dt 22:20-21","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Deut.22.20-21","rawQueryValue":"Deut.22.20-21","sourceRefExact":"Deut.22.20-21"},{"anchorText":"Jer 16:2","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Jer.16.2","rawQueryValue":"Jer.16.2","sourceRefExact":"Jer.16.2"},{"anchorText":"Jgs 11:37","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Judg.11.37","rawQueryValue":"Judg.11.37","sourceRefExact":"Judg.11.37"},{"anchorText":"1 Cor 7:7, 25-38","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Cor.7.7,25-38","rawQueryValue":"1Cor.7.7,25-38","sourceRefExact":"1Cor.7.7,25-38"},{"anchorText":"Mt 19:12","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Matt.19.12","rawQueryValue":"Matt.19.12","sourceRefExact":"Matt.19.12"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"efda8f324880066d0a690781e5c5a4b13eb9010118b11eb1b174192405f87d5b","sourceItemName":"Virgin","sourceItemOrder":24,"sourceMember":"Articles/V.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Virgin","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Virgin","title":"Virgin","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}